{"name":"Cape Cod Bay","hex":"#557080","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cape Cod Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large bay of the Atlantic Ocean adjacent to the state of Massachusetts, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cape_Cod_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape Cod Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Cape Cod Bay is a large bay of the Atlantic Ocean adjacent to the U.S. state of Massachusetts. Measuring 604 square miles (1,560 km2) below a line drawn from Brant Rock in Marshfield to Race Point in Provincetown, Massachusetts, it is enclosed by Cape Cod to the south and east, and Plymouth County, Massachusetts, to the west. To the north of Cape Cod Bay lie Massachusetts Bay and the Atlantic Ocean. Cape Cod Bay is the southernmost extremity of the Gulf of Maine. Cape Cod Bay is one of the bays adjacent to Massachusetts that give it the name Bay State. The others are Narragansett Bay, Buzzards Bay, and Massachusetts Bay."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cape_Cod_Bay_map.png/330px-Cape_Cod_Bay_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Cod_Bay","wikidata":"Q516993"},{"title":"Cape Cod","blocks":[{"text":"Cape Cod is a peninsula extending into the Atlantic Ocean from the southeastern corner of Massachusetts, in the northeastern United States. Its historic, maritime character and ample beaches attract heavy tourism during the summer months. The name Cape Cod, coined in 1602 by Bartholomew Gosnold, is the ninth-oldest English place-name in the U.S."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/White_Crest_Beach_Wellfleet.jpg/330px-White_Crest_Beach_Wellfleet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Cod","wikidata":"Q49152"},{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape","wikidata":"Q1034198"},{"title":"Cod","blocks":[{"text":"Cod is the common name for the demersal fish genus Gadus, belonging to the family Gadidae. Cod is also used as part of the common name for several other fish species, and one species that belongs to genus Gadus is not commonly called cod."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG/330px-Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cod","wikidata":"Q13194939"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg/500px-ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg/1280px-ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg/500px-ISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cape Cod, Cape Cod Bay, and Massachusetts Bay, north is oriented to the right in this photo taken from the International Space Station on June 15, 2022","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS067-E-134796_Cape_Cod.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b7/Cape_Cod_Bay_2009.jpg/500px-Cape_Cod_Bay_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b7/Cape_Cod_Bay_